.TH CYAML_DECLARE_SCOPED 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
cyaml_declare_scoped \- declare a cyaml variable with automatic RAII destruction
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cyaml.h>

cyaml_declare_scoped(var_name);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Declare a cyaml handle variable with the name var_name and set it to
NULL.  This macro also attaches a cleanup attribute to the variable.
The cleanup frees the tree that the variable holds recursively, exactly
as cyaml_destroy() does.  It runs when var_name goes out of scope, and
it leaves the variable NULL.

The cleanup runs at the end of the enclosing block, in the reverse of
the declaration order.  It runs when the block exits normally.  It also
runs when the block exits through break, continue, return or goto.

This is a GCC and Clang extension.  MSVC does not have it.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
var_name  Name of the variable to declare.
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
{
    cyaml_declare_scoped(doc);
    doc = cyaml_parse("x: 1\en", NULL);
    if (!doc) return;
    /* ... use doc ... */
}  /* doc is freed automatically here */
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cyaml_declare (3),
.BR cyaml_destroy (3)
